        															<div class="mb-4 text-gray-600 fw-bold fs-6 ps-10">Once a memory error has been detected, determining the failing module is not a clear-cut procedure. If your computer is overclocked, you should try again at default settings first. Then, if you have more than one memory module, try removing them one at a time to find the faulty one. You can also rotate them. For more informations, look <a href='https://memtest.org/readme#trouble-shooting-memory-errors'>here</a> </div>
